{
  "id": "pattern-vision",
  "term": "pattern vision",
  "definition": "Pattern vision is the aspect of seeing that allows the visual system to detect contours or edges and combine them into coherent shapes and objects. It relies on organizing visual input using cues such as proximity, collinearity, and closure so that separate parts of a scene are perceived as meaningful patterns.",
